  "text": "ordinarium.nobis-quoque",
  "about": "At “Nobis quoque peccatóribus” the rubric directs the priest to raise his voice a little and strike his breast. The prayer asks that God's sinful servants be admitted to fellowship with the Saints.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "narrative": "The priest strikes his breast with his right hand and says, with his voice raised a little:" },
    "s02": { "translation": "To us also, sinners,", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 27–28", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 69–70", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 93", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s03": { "narrative": "The priest spreads his hands as before and goes on silently." },
    "s04": { "translation": "Your servants who trust in Your abundant mercies, be pleased to bestow some portion and communion with Your holy Apostles and Martyrs:", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 27–28", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 69–70", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 93", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s05": { "translation": "with John, Stephen, Matthias, Barnabas, Ignatius, Alexander, Marcellinus, Peter, Felicity, Perpetua, Agatha, Lucy, Agnes, Cecilia, Anastasia, and all Your saints:", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 27–28", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 69–70", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 93", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s06": { "translation": "Admit us, we implore You, into their fellowship, not weighing merit but granting pardon.", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 27–28", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 69–70", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 93", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s07": { "narrative": "The priest joins his hands." },
    "s08": { "translation": "Through Christ our Lord.", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 27–28", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 69–70", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 93", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] }
  },
